index d52f73f..296efc7 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -366,6 +366,22 @@ curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/v1/audio/speech \
   --output speech.wav
 ```
 
+For the `avspeech` engine, `voice` accepts a display name (case-insensitive, e.g. `Samantha`) or a full identifier (e.g. `com.apple.voice.enhanced.en-US.Samantha`). Identifiers are the only way to disambiguate voices that share a name across languages or quality tiers.
+
+### Voice discovery
+
+```
+GET /v1/audio/voices          → {"voices": ["<id>", ...]}
+GET /v1/audio/voices/all      → {"voices": [{"id", "name", "lang", "quality"}, ...]}
+GET /v1/models                → OpenAI-style static model list (health check)
+```
+
+`quality` is `default`, `enhanced`, or `premium` (AVSpeech reports the tier of each installed system voice; download higher tiers in System Settings → Accessibility → Spoken Content → System Voices).
+
+### TTS-only deployments
+
+Set `stt: engine: none` to skip ASR model loading entirely (no downloads, instant startup). Transcription endpoints then return `503`.
+
 ## Compatible apps
 
 The HTTP API is compatible with any app or library that supports a configurable OpenAI base URL. No real API key is needed -- the server ignores `Authorization` headers, so enter any non-empty string.
